# Context filter for `docker buildx build --file web/Dockerfile .`
# BuildKit prefers <dockerfile>.dockerignore over the root .dockerignore, so
# this narrows the web image's context to the frontend without affecting the
# backend image, which shares the same context (`.`).
#
# Why it matters: the web build's layer cache is keyed on the context it copies.
# With the root .dockerignore, a backend-only commit changed the context and
# busted the Nuxt build layer, forcing a full rebuild for no reason.
**/node_modules
**/.nuxt
**/.output
**/.turbo
**/.next
.git
.github
.husky
.claude
.conductor
.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Not part of the frontend build
backend
infra
conf
postgres
scripts
docker-compose*.yml
*.md
.env*
setup.sh
